Description: drm: Release a stereo pair's waiting frame when the pair can no longer complete
 The first output of a pair to present keeps its frame until its partner
 presents, so that both go out in one commit. When the pair was undone,
 the partner was removed, disabled or turned off before that, the frame
 stayed in the pending list forever: that output's render loop waited for
 it and the output never showed a new frame again.
 .
 Drop the waiting frame when either output leaves the pair, is removed,
 or changes its enabled or power state, and when an output that is no
 longer paired presents. Dropping the frame lets its render loop go on.
